# `out += "<li>" + names[i] + "</li>"` makes no rope for the right side: the three parts go into the buffer one after the other. The literals are stores of immediates (0x3e696c3c is "<li>"), the name is copied by one stub. The stub may move the characters, so the limit of the buffer is read once a turn, behind it.
# CHECK-LABEL: steps by 1
# CHECK: Int64 b@[[name]] = Load(b@{{*}}, ControlDependent|Reads:indexedContiguousProperties, {{*}}:GetArrayElement)
# CHECK: Store($1047096380(b@{{*}}), b@[[cursor]], ControlDependent|Writes:stringBuilderBytes, {{*}}:StringBuilderAppendConstant)
# CHECK-NOT: Reads:AOTStackStringBuilder_fields
# CHECK: Int64 b@[[behindName]] = Patchpoint(b@{{*}}:Register({{*}}), b@{{*}}:Register({{*}}), b@[[name]]:Register({{*}}), resultConstraints = Register({{*}}:StringBuilderAppendString)
# CHECK: Int64 b@[[limit]] = Load(b@{{*}}, ControlDependent|Reads:AOTStackStringBuilder_fields, {{*}}:StringBuilderAppendString)
# CHECK: Store($268056670012(b@{{*}}), b@[[behindName]], ControlDependent|Writes:stringBuilderBytes, {{*}}:StringBuilderAppendConstant)
# CHECK: Int64 b@[[behindAll]] = Add(b@[[behindName]], $5(
# CHECK-NOT: Reads:AOTStackStringBuilder_fields
# CHECK: Int32 b@[[fits]] = {{*}}Equal(b@{{*}}, b@{{*}}, {{*}}:StringBuilderAppendConstant)
# CHECK-NEXT: Branch(b@[[fits]], Terminal,
# CHECK-LABEL: end of loop
# The stub is the one call of a turn that is not rare. No cell is made or loaded for either literal.
# HOT-LABEL: steps by 1
# HOT-NOT: Reads:AOTInstance_stringCells
# HOT-NOT: :String)
# HOT-LABEL: end of loop
# CALLS-LABEL: f1: size=
# CALLS-NOT: Concatenate
# CALLS: stub StackStringBuilderAppendString x1
# CALLS-NEXT: f{{*}}: size=
